---
// src/components/FAQSection.astro
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why should I hire FSI instead of getting a free inspection from a foundation repair company?",
    a: "A foundation repair company has an inherent conflict of interest: they generate revenue by selling you steel or concrete piers costing thousands of dollars. FSI does NOT sell foundation repairs. We are state-licensed Professional Engineers whose sole obligation is the scientific, unbiased truth. Over half the homes we inspect require no structural underpinning whatsoever."
  },
  {
    q: "How quickly can I receive my engineering report?",
    a: "We offer same-day engineering reports throughout the DFW metroplex. We understand that Texas real estate option periods are typically only 3 to 7 days, so we prioritize rapid data collection, CAD generation, and PE stamping to deliver your report on the same day as the physical inspection."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the difference between a standard home inspector and a Professional Engineer (PE)?",
    a: "Standard home inspectors have general knowledge but cannot legally render structural engineering opinions, calculate load-bearing stresses, or stamp structural repair drawings. If a home inspector suspects foundation issues, they are required by Texas law to recommend an evaluation by a licensed Professional Engineer. FSI provides the definitive, certified PE stamp that lenders, title companies, and city permit offices require."
  },
  {
    q: "What equipment do you use during an inspection?",
    a: "In addition to a comprehensive visual audit of exterior brick, fascia, trim, interior walls, and framing, we use high-precision digital manometers. This electronic floor survey maps the elevation contours of your slab down to ±0.01 inches, revealing the exact differential settlement of your foundation."
  },
  {
    q: "Do your reports include CAD drawings?",
    a: "Yes. Every comprehensive inspection includes detailed CAD elevation drawings and structural framing maps, illustrating floor level deviations and structural components ready for city permits or contractor bidding."
  },
  {
    q: "What areas of DFW do you service?",
    a: "We provide foundation and structural inspection services throughout the entire Dallas-Fort Worth Metroplex and surrounding counties, including Dallas, Tarrant, Collin, Denton, Rockwall, and Kaufman counties."
  }
];
---

<section class="py-24 bg-[#070B14] text-white relative" id="faq">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-start">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Sticky Context Card (4 Cols) -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-4 lg:sticky lg:top-28 space-y-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 border border-blue-400/20 text-blue-300 text-xs font-telemetry uppercase tracking-wider">
          Engineering Inquiries
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">
          Frequently Asked Questions.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Everything you need to know about independent structural engineering evaluations, option-period deadlines, and certified PE stamps in North Texas.
        </p>

        <!-- Direct Contact Card -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl glass-card border border-slate-700/80 space-y-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-telemetry uppercase text-slate-400">Have an urgent transaction question?</p>
          <a 
            href="mailto:Info@foundationstructureinspection.com" 
            class="text-sm font-bold text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors block break-all font-telemetry"
          >
            Info@foundationstructureinspection.com
          </a>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-telemetry">
            Mon–Sat: 8:00 AM – 6:00 PM
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: Accordion Matrix (8 Cols) -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-4">
        {faqs.map((faq, idx) => (
          <details class="glass-card rounded-2xl p-6 border border-slate-700/80 group transition-all" open={idx === 0}>
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white group-hover:text-blue-400 transition-colors">
              <span>{faq.q}</span>
              <span class="ml-4 w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-slate-800 text-slate-300 flex items-center justify-center text-xs group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 font-telemetry">
                ▼
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800/80 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              {faq.a}
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
